## Exp40 — Multi-Horizon Active-Corridor Competing-Risk Family — COMPLETED / FULL PASS

### Frozen question

Does the information in the CURRENT ACTIVE corridor persist beyond one M5 transition at fixed horizons `15m / 30m / 60m / 120m`?

Frozen competing-risk target from every exact Exp20/21 starting state:

```text
NO_EXIT
ADVANCE first by future M5 CLOSE
RECAPTURE first by future M5 CLOSE
```

Starting L1-L2 boundaries remain fixed for the state. Cells are censored if the future path becomes unobservable before the target is determined. Primary estimand is pooled `STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED`; whole BRT days are resampled preserving all state-horizon cells from each sampled day.

Models are fit separately by horizon using TRAIN only:

```text
CONST_H
POSITION_H = geo_logit(CorridorPosition)
SEMI_H     = geo_logit(CorridorPosition) + log1p(DwellBars)
```

### Exact reproduction and coverage

All Exp20/21 upstream and split guards reproduced exactly before Exp40 scoring.

Coverage strongly exceeded the frozen 70% floor:

```text
TRAIN      21681/22448 cells = 96.58%; all-4 states 5220/5612 = 93.01%
VALIDATION  7577/ 7836 cells = 96.69%; all-4 states 1831/1959 = 93.47%
TEST        8008/ 8384 cells = 95.52%; all-4 states 1898/2096 = 90.55%
```

Censoring was driven by M5 gaps and rose smoothly with horizon. TEST eligibility remained 99.05% at 15m and 90.55% at 120m.

### Observed competing-risk depth

TEST:

```text
15m  NO_EXIT 77.50% | ADV  8.48% | REC 14.02%
30m  NO_EXIT 64.47% | ADV 14.17% | REC 21.36%
60m  NO_EXIT 50.30% | ADV 21.08% | REC 28.62%
120m NO_EXIT 33.14% | ADV 28.87% | REC 37.99%
```

### TRAIN coefficient structure

Position preserved the expected side geometry at every horizon: ADV geo coefficient positive and REC geo coefficient negative. Magnitudes attenuated with horizon.

Dwell coefficients were negative for BOTH causes at every horizon:

```text
H=15m  ADV dwell=-0.691865 | REC dwell=-0.525664
H=30m  ADV dwell=-0.708940 | REC dwell=-0.519087
H=60m  ADV dwell=-0.754371 | REC dwell=-0.580955
H=120m ADV dwell=-0.714698 | REC dwell=-0.593600
```

This is a stable duration-dependence signature: after current position is known, older surviving corridor states have lower cumulative exit propensity over the next fixed horizon.

### Horizon diagnostics

Every frozen horizon showed positive POSITION-vs-CONST and SEMI-vs-POSITION point gains in Validation and TEST. No horizon selection is permitted.

TEST point gains:

```text
15m  POS-CONST Brier +0.035063 | LL +0.110230 | SEMI-POS Brier +0.025171 | LL +0.050423
30m  POS-CONST Brier +0.054507 | LL +0.133559 | SEMI-POS Brier +0.052732 | LL +0.077141
60m  POS-CONST Brier +0.082683 | LL +0.153757 | SEMI-POS Brier +0.058615 | LL +0.081603
120m POS-CONST Brier +0.095192 | LL +0.140869 | SEMI-POS Brier +0.044346 | LL +0.071952
```

### Pooled proper scores

```text
VALIDATION
CONST     Brier 0.551099198 | LL 0.934900431
POSITION  Brier 0.482576694 | LL 0.811772319
SEMI      Brier 0.453998308 | LL 0.761253616

TEST
