Important non-retroactivity rule: Exp40 does NOT retroactively change the formal Exp21 one-step verdict. Exp21 remains positive but not fully strictly reconfirmed because the frozen Exp26 Validation state-weighted Brier CI crossed zero. Exp40 establishes a separate multi-horizon Dwell result under a different target family.

### Mechanistic diagnostics

Adding Dwell greatly improves EXIT discrimination while barely changing EXIT-side discrimination:

```text
VALIDATION EXIT AUC delta: +0.0742 / +0.0857 / +0.1066 / +0.0804 for 15/30/60/120m
TEST       EXIT AUC delta: +0.1152 / +0.1494 / +0.1388 / +0.1357
```

SIDE AUC changes are near zero. This strongly supports the existing factorization:

```text
CorridorPosition -> WHICH SIDE
Dwell            -> WHEN / WHETHER EXIT within horizon
```

Despite independent fitting by horizon, predicted `P(NO_EXIT)` was already nearly perfectly non-increasing across horizons: approximately 99.95% in Validation and TEST for SEMI.

### DNA update after Exp40

The strongest current Track-D representation is now:

```text
ACTIVE STRUCTURAL FRONTIER
  -> CURRENT ACTIVE CORRIDOR
     -> CorridorPosition  [strong core; side geometry; multi-horizon depth]
     -> Dwell             [duration/hazard coordinate; multi-horizon depth]
     -> competing-risk future {NO_EXIT, ADVANCE, RECAPTURE}
```

The evidence now argues against interpreting Position+Dwell as merely a next-M5 artifact. The same two-coordinate state representation carries substantial proper-score information across 15-120 minutes in historical OOS.

Anti-overstatement:
- TEST is repeatedly inspected;
- costs/slippage are irrelevant to this structural probability experiment and were not modeled;
- Exp40 is not a trading-rule backtest;
- no runtime rule/model promotion is authorized;
- fresh forward Exp27 remains the decisive prospective gate.

